[Music]  britain's prince andrew faces a  potential lawsuit in the u.s over  allegations that he sexually abused a 17  year old girl in the early 2000s these  allegations stem from his long-standing  friendship with gelane maxwell a  socialite who is closely connected to  convicted sex offender jeffrey epstein  the lawsuit comes at a complicated time  for the british monarchy and if a trial  goes forward it could coincide with a  queen celebration of 70 years on the  throne  the prince could settle and so this  trial might not go ahead at all but if  it does there is the risk that andrew  will have to be cross-examined by  lawyers and may reveal embarrassing  details about the alleged events that  took place in the early 2000s  the real question here is if if there is  a financial settlement who's actually  pay buckingham palace will have to  navigate that very very very carefully  because if it is seen to be the british  taxpayer who's picking up any of the  bill for this there could be a huge  public backlash  the allegations brought against prince  andrew have been swirling for years a  woman named virginia gefray alleges in a  lawsuit that she was forced to have sex  with prince andrew when she was 17.  she claims she was trafficked by epstein  and maxwell that the prince was aware of  that fact and that he abused her in  london new york and on epstein's private  island  juffrey filed the lawsuit against prince  andrew last year he has denied all  allegations  in 2019 prince andrew did an interview  with the bbc during which he said he was  friends with jeffrey epstein he also  said that he and epstein weren't very  close and that he had never met jufree  i have no recollection of ever meeting  this lady  none whatsoever you don't remember  meeting her and he was presented this  this photo which is now well known of  him with his arm around mr frey and he  said he had no recollection of that  photo being taken and since then he's  not said anything really publicly  jeffrey epstein died in jail while  awaiting trial on sex trafficking  charges in 2019 and in december 2021  guillen maxwell was found guilty on  criminal counts of sex trafficking if it  goes ahead prince andrew's trial on the  civil suit could take place in the fall  one of the big issues here is that a  trial could be reputationally damaging  for for prince andrew for the monarchy  but also for prince andrew's direct  family and that means that there is a  big big incentive here for him to just  pay to make this go away and that's the  that's the most likely outcome  lawyers say but the big question is what  mr frey will ask for in return because  it might not just be money it may also  be some form of apology  cut off from his royal duties prince  andrew has lost much of his income and  there's uncertainty over how he might  pay for a potentially expensive  settlement  according to royal biographers prince  andrew still has a pension from the navy  and owns a chalet in switzerland that is  up for sale buckingham palace didn't  immediately respond to a request for  comment about his assets the financial  risk he faces that he is unemployed he  is someone who has no job and so  therefore will presumably be relying on  his mother  or any wealth he accumulated before to  kind of pay his way from now on  this is all threatening the monarchy's  image at a delicate time  after it became clear in early 2022 that  the lawsuit could proceed to trial  buckingham palace stripped the prince of  his military titles and patronages and  announced he would no longer use the  title his royal highness  he is still a prince he is still the  duke of york but he is no longer his  royal highness and he no longer has any  role to play in the sort of ceremonial  duties of monarchy prince andrew isn't  the only royal this has happened to most  recently prince harry and his wife  meghan markle agreed not to use their  royal highness titles when they quit the  royal fam  harry was also stripped of his military  affiliations  as the royal family works to defuse  reputational damage from these recent  incidents it's also being faced with the  challenge of preparing for the eventual  passing of queen elizabeth she turns 96  this year and has already stepped back  slightly from public duties her son  charles and grandson prince william have  as a result been stepping up more  prince andrew now is effectively  holed up on his mother's estate in  windsor  plotting his defense as a private  citizen  in a way he is now a sort of prince  without a role he's in a sort of  semi-exile  and it really depends how this court  case plays out i mean some question that  even if he did manage to clear his name  or settle with virginia dufresne he  would  always be tainted by association given  his friendship with maxwell and epstein  and that means that it'll be very hard  for him to ever be rehabilitated

